  "question": {
    "text": "A current of dry air was passed first through a series of bulbs containing a solution of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> in ethanol of molality 0.725 and then through a series of bulbs containing pure ethanol. (T = 284 K) loss in weight of the solvent bulbs was 0.0685 g. Calculate the loss in weight of the solution bulbs.",
    "image": null
  },
